{"id":"classes-established-then-filled","title":"Classes created by a classification action, and who filled them","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"When Human Resources established a new job class, how soon was anyone paid in it, how many people, and where had they been before?","finding":"Classification actions established 171 job classes between fiscal 2015 and 2026. 80 were first paid in the fiscal year of the action or the next; 42 of those started with one or two holders and 31 with exactly one, and 6 of the small ones went to people not on the payroll the year before. 66 have never had a paid holder, and 7 already had paid holders before the action, which marks a class being re-established or renumbered.","how":"The Department of Human Resources’ lists of classification actions, fiscal 2009 to 2027 (the index lists none for fiscal 2013-14), name the class codes each action established, amended, retitled or abolished; this screen takes every code with an action whose wording includes “Establish” in fiscal 2015 to 2026 and looks up the first fiscal year anyone was paid in it in the City payroll. The origination date is the one printed on the class’s own page, where there is one. First holders are named only from fiscal 2017 and only for classes that began with one or two; their earlier job is read from the payroll by name under the matching rules. Classes filled within a year by one or two people come first, by rate of pay. Lists before fiscal 2025 give codes without titles, so titles are the payroll’s.","limits":"The action lists do not say which department asked for the class or why, and the notices do not say either: those for fiscal 2009 to 2016, saved on 25 November 2026, name a department only when they allocate a management position. A class number that was abolished and later reused is dated from the first Establish after its last Abolish. A class established and never paid may be filled under another class number, or may belong to a body outside the payroll file. The fiscal year of an action is known, not its day, so “within a year” is to the fiscal year.","columns":[{"k":"job","t":"Job class","type":"text"},{"k":"established","t":"Fiscal year of the action","type":"year"},{"k":"origin","t":"Origin date on the class page","type":"text"},{"k":"firstPaid","t":"First fiscal year paid","type":"year"},{"k":"lag","t":"Years between","type":"int"},{"k":"holders","t":"Holders that year","type":"int"},{"k":"holder","t":"First holder","type":"person"},{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"before","t":"The year before (by name)","type":"text"},{"k":"type","t":"Type of appointment","type":"text"},{"k":"now","t":"Since","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"job":"Physician Administrator, DPH (class 1167)","established":2016,"origin":"1 July 2016","firstPaid":2017,"lag":1,"holders":1,"holder":"Susan Ehrlich","department":"Public Health","before":"","type":"Permanent Exempt","now":"1 holder in fiscal 2026"},{"job":"Chief Medical Examiner (class 2584)","established":2021,"origin":"12 January 1964","firstPaid":2021,"lag":0,"holders":1,"holder":"Christopher Liverman","department":"City Administrator","before":"Not on the payroll the year before","type":"Permanent Exempt","now":"1 holder in fiscal 2026"},{"job":"Transitional Department Head (class 0971)","established":2016,"origin":"16 May 2016","firstPaid":2017,"lag":1,"holders":1,"holder":"John Martin","department":"Airport Commission","before":"","type":"Permanent Exempt","now":"4 holders in fiscal 2026"},{"job":"Inspector General, CON (class 1688)","established":2025,"origin":"11 April 2025","firstPaid":2026,"lag":1,"holders":1,"holder":"Alexandra Shepard","department":"Controller","before":"Not on the payroll the year before","type":"Permanent Exempt","now":"1 holder in fiscal 2026"},{"job":"Technology Expert II (class 9978)","established":2016,"origin":"15 June 2016","firstPaid":2017,"lag":1,"holders":2,"holder":"David Nelson; Lori Wallace","department":"Public Health","befor